{"availability":"available","full":"ikigai-rs/ikigai-web-demo","name":"ikigai-web-demo","description":"The ikigai resolution kernel running in the browser via WebAssembly — a page assembled by client-side resource resolution, no server.","category":"Other","language":"Rust","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-06-15T04:12:42Z","updated":"2026-10-07T22:41:02Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://ikigai-rs.github.io/ikigai-web-demo/","topics":["browser","demo","ikigai","rdf","resource-oriented","resource-oriented-computing","rust","wasm","webassembly"],"demo":"https://crates.io/crates/ikigai-core","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T03:23:50.145Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T03:23:50.145Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T03:23:50.145Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T03:23:50.145Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The ikigai resolution kernel running in the browser via WebAssembly — no server, no fetch, no JS framework.","The page is a resource. index.html is a near-empty shell that makes one call — compose('urn:data:page') — and drops the result into the body. The kernel resolves the page shape (HTML) and recursively expands every $a{} transclusion marker in it, resolving each embedded resource through the kernel; a marker may carry arguments ($a{urn:iki:fn:toUpper?in=\"resource-oriented computing\"}) and a transcluded shape may contain further markers, so composition recurses. Resolution, the endpoints, the compose builtin, and the content-addressed cache all run client-side in WASM. The client is 5 lines of…","The page even carries a live terminal — the same renderer-agnostic Engine the desktop ikigai REPL uses, compiled to WASM and driving this page's kernel. It's mounted by composition too: a $a{urn:demo:web-cli} marker in the page shape resolves to an element that wires itself up on insertion. Because it shares the page's kernel and content-addressed cache, typing source urn:iki:fn:compose src=urn:data:page into it returns the very page you're reading — reported cached, since the page already composed it. The whole grammar works in the browser: pipelines |, map .., fork ( a ; b ), named…"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ikigai-rs/ikigai-web-demo/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"7273d81e34633f57e1a682a52dae242b01d186c7efcc3426a3469ae739425769","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T03:23:50.249Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T03:23:50.249Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The ikigai resolution kernel running in the browser via WebAssembly — no server, no fetch, no JS framework.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ikigai-rs/ikigai-web-demo/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"7273d81e34633f57e1a682a52dae242b01d186c7efcc3426a3469ae739425769","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ikigai-rs/ikigai-web-demo/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T03:23:50.249Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-07T22:41:02Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ikigai-rs/ikigai-web-demo/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T03:23:50.249Z","hash":"7273d81e34633f57e1a682a52dae242b01d186c7efcc3426a3469ae739425769","originalBytes":9661,"storedBytes":9661,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["page","urn","kernel","same","wasm","demo","dist","one","over","cache","compose","run","source","toupper","each","iki","ikigai","server","target","two","which","about","browser","cached","cert","crate","file","host","live","marker","names","open","own","session","shacl","table","webtransport","build","cap","capability","cargo","composed","composes","composition","crates","data","engine","entry","glue","hello","http","list","module","needs","never","published","release","rule","src","steps","still","under","via","wasm-bindgen","wasm32-unknown-unknown","write","above","aliases","already","anything","back","bash","because","bin","binds","box","cannot","cli","client-side","comes","c